        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2069c2a2-138e-5cb6-96e9-6175ab403eb1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking, New South Wales Government, New South Wales Police, The Honoured Society, Mafia\n- Places: New South Wales, Australia, Sydney\n- Events: Wodward Royal Commission\n- Concepts: Drug trafficking, police-crime links, 'Ndrangheta\n\nFacts:\n- From 1977 to 1979, the Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking operated as a royal commission in New South Wales, Australia.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking was also known as the Wodward Royal Commission.\n- The New South Wales Government initiated the Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking to investigate drug trafficking in New South Wales.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking especially examined links between the New South Wales Police and the Mafia.\n- The Honoured Society is a Calabrian 'Ndrangheta criminal confederation.\n- The Honoured Society started in Sydney.\n- The Honoured Society is currently active across Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8ae2cc5d-0892-5541-b1e7-34067b5c761d",
        "text": "The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking (1977-1979) or Wodward Royal Commission was a royal commission initiated by the New South Wales Government to investigate drug trafficking in New South Wales, Australia, especially links between the New South Wales Police and Mafia, The Honoured Society, is a Calabrian 'Ndrangheta criminal confederation, started in Sydney and currently active in all of Australia.",
